november is nearing which means the next  generation of consoles is  almost here so let's get you all caught  up with a round out of what's in the  boxes  what they're gonna play and when you can  get your hands on them here's everything  you'll need to know about microsoft's  minimalist mini-fridge and sony's  curvaceous popped collar box in order to  compare the two  first up let's do the bit with all the  important numbers  the playstation 5 is fitted with eight  amd zen 2 cpu cores  clocked at a variable frequency of 3.5  gigahertz  comparatively the xbox series x has the  same amd processor  but it's clocked slightly higher at 3.8  gigahertz  in terms of graphics sony's box offers  up 10.3 teraflops  and 36 cus clocked at a variable  frequency of 2.23 gigahertz  while the series x runs with 12.16  teraflops  and 52 cus clocked at 1.825 gigahertz  both boxes are packed with 16 gigabytes  of gddr6 sd  ram a 4k uhd blu-ray optical drive  assuming you opt for the disc included  version of the ps5  a max output resolution of 8k and a  maximum refresh rate of 120 hertz  in terms of storage you should see a  noticeable improvement in load times as  the ps5 comes with an 825 gigabyte ssd  and the xbox series x comes with a one  terabyte ssd  as games continue to get bigger that's  something that may concern you  though both consoles do have slots for  expandable storage  specifically an nvme slot in the ps5  and a one terabyte microsoft expansion  card slot in the series  x it's also worth mentioning that if  you're thinking of opting for the xbox  series s  which only comes with a 512 gigabyte ssd  microsoft is helping you out by making  games up to 30  smaller for the console and so they'll  take up less space  if that's all greek to you don't worry  basically the specs are pretty darn  similar although the xbox series x does  take a slight technical advantage  the most interesting differences are  that at launch the ps5 will only offer  backwards compatibility with the ps4  while series x will be backwards  compatible with the xbox  xbox 360 and xbox one that said the ps5  is launching with vr support while it's  sounding less and less likely that the  series x will do the same  according to a sound byte from xbox boss  phil spencer last year where he said  we're responding to what our customers  are asking for and nobody's asking for  vr  both consoles also support ray tracing  which enables them to better simulate  light in games  and most importantly both are a serious  upgrade over their predecessors  so that's the two boxes covered now  let's dig into the all-important  controllers  the ps5's dual sense controller looks to  be quite a bit different to the ps4s  dualshock 4.  the controller includes haptic feedback  adaptive triggers that can add  resistance based on the game  as well as a speaker and touchpad much  like that of the dualshock 4.  it's a little chunkier than its sibling  so if you're a playstation fan who  always hoped sony would add a little  more bulk to their controllers  this could be right up your alley as for  the xbox series x its controller is a  little smaller than its predecessor but  otherwise it's almost  identical the only new things of note  are a share button and a hybrid 4-way  and 8-way directional pad  your xbox one controllers will also work  on series x  and your series x controller can be used  on xbox one  comparatively while the dualshock 4 can  be used on ps5 to play ps4 games with  backwards compatibility  you won't be able to use it to play ps5  games  xbox live gold and playstation plus are  making a return but things get a little  more complicated than that for next gen  microsoft have confirmed that both the  xbox series x and  sirius s will be available through  xbox's all-access subscription  service here you can pay 25 usd a month  for series s  or 35 usd a month for the series x over  a period of 24 months  and you'll also get game pass ultimate  included that's a combo of game pass for  both xbox and pc  ea play xcloud and xbox live gold  for the ps5 sony has revealed the plus  collection a library of some of the  ps4's best games that will be freely  available to plus subscribers  the collection includes games like god  of war bloodborne days gone persona 5  and resident evil 7.  the plus collection is exclusive to the  ps5 while it's certainly not as beefy of  an offering as microsoft's xbox game  pass  there's some really good stuff in there  so check out the full list in our story  on gamespot  as for gaming on the cloud if that's  your thing ps5 will presumably continue  to offer its playstation now service  and xbox series x will work with  microsoft project xcloud  as the service is bundled with xbox game  pass ultimate  now we're sufficiently covered up on how  you'll be playing the games  let's dig into what shall we playing  xbox series x will support smart  delivery for select titles where you can  download a series x  optimized version of a game for free if  you own it on xbox one  smart delivery titles include cyberpunk  2077  assassin's creed valhalla chorus and  yakuza like a dragon  outside of smart delivery the xbox  series x launch lineup includes gears  tactics  nba 2k 21 fifa 21 and fortnite  in 2021 and beyond xbox series x is  scheduled to get halo infinite  forza motorsport the ascent and senegal  saga hellblade 2.  on the playstation side launch titles  will include spider-man miles morales  the demon souls remake sac boy a big  adventure  astros playroom assassin's creed  valhalla destruction all-stars  and fortnite console exclusives arriving  on the platform later on will include  horizon forbidden west  ratchet and clank rift apart and of  course bug snacks  if you're looking for more complete  lists of what you can play on next  generation consoles  do check out our videos covering off on  every game coming to ps5  and xbox series x respectively as for  the all-important release date and price  point the xbox series x is due out on  november 10th  and will run you 499 bucks in the us  while the playstation 5 will also run  you 499 bucks  and 399 for its diskless version  it's out on november the 12th  microsoft's tiny less powerful diskless  offering the xbox series s  will also be available on november 10th  but for 299 dollars in the us  250 pounds in the uk and 499  in australia you're probably not from  australia but i just wanted you to know  consoles are expensive here  pre-orders for microsoft's next-gen  consoles alive on september 22nd while  ps5 pre-orders are live now if you can  manage to find somebody with stock  let me know down in that comment box if  you're planning on getting a next  generation console which one  and why as always we'll keep you covered  off on everything ps5  xbox series x and everything else that  matters in gaming  you
 

